Shared Responsibilities
ERD: Each member designs 6 tables. All sections will be combined into one unified ERD, with consistent relationships and foreign keys.
SQL Implementation: Each member creates and populates their 6 tables with realistic data. All SQL files will be integrated into one database.
Queries: Each member develops 2 meaningful queries, for a total of 8.
Website: Each member contributes one section to a shared 1–2 page dashboard.
Analysis Report: Each member documents their design decisions, assumptions, and limitations. The sections will be combined into one report.
Presentation: Each member presents their respective portion of the project.
Final Target: 24 tables, 8 SQL queries, 1–2 web pages, one unified ERD, a populated database, and a complete analysis report.

Team Statement:
Work will be divided equally among the four group members, with each person responsible for one section of the hotel database system. Each member will design six ERD tables, implement and populate their tables in SQL, develop two meaningful queries, contribute to the web interface, and write their portion of the analysis report.
To maintain accountability, we will establish internal deadlines, track individual progress through a shared GitHub repository, and hold regular meetups to review completed work and identify any difficulties. We will communicate openly in our group chat and assist one another with technical challenges, particularly when integrating different sections of the database.
To prevent an uneven workload, we will periodically review each member's responsibilities and redistribute tasks if certain sections require significantly more time or effort than anticipated. All members will also participate in reviewing, testing, and finalizing the project to ensure that contributions remain balanced throughout the process.
